1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,655
Welcome to StormSignal.

2
00:00:02,835 --> 00:00:11,070
When severe weather affects a trip, travellers
need to find reliable warnings and clear next
steps quickly.

3
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:21,070
This prototype gives people across India a
simple starting point for official weather
information and practical travel safety
guidance.

4
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:27,805
For district weather warnings, open the India
Meteorological Department map.

5
00:00:27,985 --> 00:00:36,710
Choose your forecast date and district directly
on the official IMD page, then read the warning
published there.

6
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:43,530
The map shows several forecast days, and the
latest available dates can change.

7
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:50,965
StormSignal links to the source; it does not
copy changing warning data into this app.

8
00:00:51,145 --> 00:00:57,950
For current disaster alerts, StormSignal also
links to NDMA SACHET.

9
00:00:58,130 --> 00:01:04,925
Check that official page for current alert
details and instructions from the issuing
authority.

10
00:01:05,105 --> 00:01:16,010
The interface and general guidance are available
in 18 languages, including twelve Indian
languages and several used by international
visitors.

11
00:01:16,190 --> 00:01:22,225
For example, you can switch between Hindi,
English, and French.

12
00:01:22,405 --> 00:01:31,775
These translations cover the StormSignal
interface and guidance; they are not
translations of the official warning itself.

13
00:01:31,955 --> 00:01:38,290
Before you travel, check the district and
forecast date for your destination.

14
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:41,855
Never walk or drive through floodwater.

15
00:01:42,035 --> 00:01:50,135
Avoid exposed places during severe weather, and
follow local shelter or evacuation instructions.

16
00:01:50,315 --> 00:01:56,250
Warnings can change, so recheck the official
source before moving.

17
00:01:56,430 --> 00:02:05,840
For police, fire, medical, and other emergency
assistance anywhere in India, call one one two.

18
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:10,050
StormSignal is not an emergency service.

19
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:14,535
Follow current instructions from local
authorities.

20
00:02:14,715 --> 00:02:27,970
The app does not track your location or show
street-level flood conditions, road closures,
verified shelters, evacuation routes, or rescue
dispatch.

21
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:37,450
Its purpose is to make it easier to reach
official information and practical safety
guidance, while keeping the source clear.

22
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:41,095
Thanks for exploring StormSignal.


